<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dyah Pitaloka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1357">1357</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Dyah Pitaloka Citraresmi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dyah Pitaloka was a princess of the Sunda Kingdom, daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linggabuana">Linggabuana</a>. In 1357 she travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> to marry King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a>, but when the chief minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a> demanded that she be handed over as a sign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a>'s submission, the Sundanese party was destroyed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bubat">Battle of Bubat</a>, and she is said to have taken her own life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dyah-pitaloka.jpg" alt="Dyah Pitaloka" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Historian128 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bubat_war_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
